  "description": "<p><b>Description</b><br/>\nThe invoice email sent from the customer portal attributes the invoice to \"Bravo Mechanical Services\" in four places. The organisation is Staging Heavy Duty - 9919. A customer receiving this sees a company that has nothing to do with their invoice.</p>\n\n<p><b>Environment</b><br/>\n<tt>staging.portal.shopview.com</tt> · org Staging Heavy Duty - 9919 · invoice S-32981</p>\n\n<p><b>Steps</b></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Portal → Invoices → open S-32981</li>\n\t<li>Click the email icon and send to yourself</li>\n\t<li>Open the email</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<p><b>Actual</b></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Subject: <em>Invoice #S-32981 - Bravo Mechanical Services</em></li>\n\t<li>Body: <em>\"Bravo Mechanical Services has shared an invoice with you\"</em></li>\n\t<li><em>\"please don't hesitate to contact Bravo Mechanical Services directly\"</em></li>\n\t<li>Footer: <em>\"Sent by ShopView on behalf of Bravo Mechanical Services\"</em></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>The attached PDF itself is correct — it shows Staging Heavy Duty - 9919.</p>\n\n<p><b>Expected</b><br/>\nThe email names the invoice's own organisation.</p>\n\n<p><b>Note for dev</b><br/>\nWorth confirming whether that string is hardcoded or read from another organisation's record. If the latter, it's a cross-tenant data issue.</p>\n\n\n<p><span class=\"image-wrap\" style=\"\"><img src=\"https://shopview.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/60628\" alt=\"image-20260912-101939.png\" width=\"865\" style=\"border: 0px solid black\" /></span></p>",
